Z||000000||RossT||01-21-2000||01:12 AM||||I know! this is totally O/T, but my refrigerator is dying. Anyone have anything good or bad to say about the most popular brands? Is maytag really worth the extra bucks? I feel strange posting such a topic here, but you guys are always honest.<P>Thanks. Ross||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-21-2000||04:27 AM||||Our Whirlpool is only 2 years old but we haven't had any problems with it.  My grandmother has a Whirlpool that's probably 20 year old and she has never had a single problem with hers!  Whirlpool is a little more expensive than some of the others, but I think it's worth it.  I just found out recently that Roper is made on the same assembly line as Whirlpool.  The only differences are that W* can be had in different colors and Roper is (I think) a white only brand.  Also, I don't think that Roper has some of the upper models with the fancy (read: expensive when they break) electronics.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||01-21-2000||05:05 AM||||Thanks for the advice monkey, The one I have now is a whirlpool. Bought it new in 1989 for 750 bucks.  The problem is that the compressor used back then was a rotary design. (very bad). It makes lots of noise when running. It will cost to much to fix it.<BR>I have been told that they now use a piston design compressor, much more reliable. So even though I am mad a whirlpool, I certainly will not rule out buying another one.  <P>any appliance repair people out there?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||01-21-2000||09:41 AM||||Ross... Kenmore used to be made by Whirlpool. Probably still are. Good stuff. We have a 2.5 year-old Amana. Works fine, but it's the noisiest d@mn refrigerator I've ever heard. Almost sounds like it's breathing.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||01-21-2000||10:10 AM||||I bought my Kenmore fridge from Sears 8 years ago and I'm quite pleased with it. I have some family members that have owned Kenmores for decades. I looked in Consumer Reports when I was buying mine and it was rated quite high at that time.||||reg||1
